{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings","id":1112862,"title":"Changeling the Dreaming without the other settings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-07T12:56:44-07:00","id":1112862,"title":"Changeling the Dreaming without the other settings","content":"We all know crossovers stink. And the different groups populating the classic World of Darkness all have their own mechanics, most of which dont mesh with Changeling.<br /> <br /> Personally, I handle the other types of beings as denizens of the Dreaming (vampires, werecritters, etc) or mortals with enough knowledge of magic to be dangerous (hedge magic and/or Arts n Realms).<br /> <br /> What house rules do you use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-07-2017, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:51:56-07:00","id":1112900,"title":"","content":"Those work well enough. The changeling mindset allows for any other critter to be emulated as either a kith or chimera. The new 'create your own kith' rules help too. In changeling lore, they're all just Prodigals anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T14:06:10-07:00","id":1112907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1112900#post1112900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those work well enough. The changeling mindset allows for any other critter to be emulated as either a kith or chimera. The new 'create your own kith' rules help too. In changeling lore, they're all just Prodigals anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And you make a good point on kith creation. Kiths like ennchanters, wolfen, and bloodfiends would be great. <br /> <br /> Fairy Animals are a good option here. Unicorns that look like deer or horses to mortals, magical badgers and talking cats to name a few. The Rorqual in particular come to mind as important fae animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-07-2017, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T17:33:55-07:00","id":1113004,"title":"","content":"I haven't had trouble using other gamelines for NPCs, as long as I own and are familiar with their respective books. Any other cosmology is secondary to Changeling's in a Changeling game. <br /> <br /> I do think Mages might work for PC mixing, but I've never tried it, and I wouldn't use any other gameline for PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T17:44:21-07:00","id":1113008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1113004#post1113004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't had trouble using other gamelines for NPCs, as long as I own and are familiar with their respective books. Any other cosmology is secondary to Changeling's in a Changeling game. <br /> <br /> I do think Mages might work for PC mixing, but I've never tried it, and I wouldn't use any other gameline for PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages outstrip all other types in short order as pcs. Personally I like fae to have the dynamic edge in magic. So I allow linear mages in Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T17:54:40-07:00","id":1113011,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure they do from my having run both games separately, but like I said I haven't tried a crossover game. I get the impression that Mages win out on flexibility, while Changelings edge out on raw magical power, for the same length of time as a PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T18:02:44-07:00","id":1113015,"title":"","content":"The possibilities for mixed Changeling/Mage games IS interesting. Though Tradition mages are an easier go-to, I am thoughtful of a fae friendly Craft. Or even Orphan mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-07-2017, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T19:14:12-07:00","id":1113050,"title":"","content":"You could be able to transmute Mages into something more &quot;Changeling&quot;<br /> <br /> If we take the short story about Mages in Changeling corebook, True Mages are some sort of powerful dreamers belonging to four factions related to the elements that created new dreams without the help of the fae.<br /> <br /> If we take this to the heart , I think it could be appropiate to treat them as humans but with Arts and Realms similar to faes. Their power it's supposed to be very Glamorous, exept for those who are servants of Banality that are the opposite. Powerful ones may be able to travel to the Dreaming and have a certain influence there, to both cement the idea that true mages are potent dreamers and to make a wink to the idea that mages may leave the earth to be immortal, and become mad or unhuman in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T22:51:39-07:00","id":1113124,"title":"","content":"Personally I've never had any troubles with crossovers, mixed PC's or just using NPC's of different lines, usually the greatest difficulties come from crossing wraiths with anything since they are usually within another realm of existence but even that can be done.<br /> <br /> That aside the four factions, or elements, that Mages are presented in the story of changeling core, 2nd edition core that is, align with the four Avatar essences. 3 of which align with the 3 core concepts of WoDs basic forces Dynamism, Stasis and Entrophy also known as Wyld, Weaver and Wyrm the fourth is the Questing Essence. But the essences themselves do not necessarily connect to how banal a Mage is as even a static traditionalist generally ends up on the lower side of the Banality scale while even the most Dynamic Technocrat will end up rather high on said scale. <br /> <br /> Power wise changelings are now, since C20, quite near if not equal to Mages in both power of effects and versatility as well, thanks to Unleashings. Though changeling power is limited by how scarce Glamour is as a resource and the pure unpredictability of Unleashings. But thanks to generally higher power dicepoools Changelings have the edge on Mages in quick and unpredictable situations while Mages still hold the edge, as always, when they have time to prepare and cast their effects with extented rituals.<br /> <br /> All this is naturally assuming that the ST is familiar enough with both lines to mix em naturally.<br /> <br /> In genral though I dont think I have any particular house rules I use though, going back to the original question posed by the OP, but with crossovers it's occasionally good to remember the golden rule and that the story comes first but then again that actually goes with any game not just crossovers.<br /> <br /> Just KISS and do not get too hung up on every little thing, in the end WoD rules tend to be quite simple and the few rules that are incompatible, like effects relying on traits like humanity, rage or some other trait specific to a game line are usually easy to manage, either by assigning an approximation of said trait or even just using a similar, but different, trait the other party does possess to just making a ruling according to the spirit of the power in question. For example of the last option if a Vampiric power uses a mechanic tied to targets humanity just consider why the power in question uses humanity as a difficulty or some other part of the mechanic and then rule the difficulty or effect accordingly. A Savage Redcap or a nightmarish Thallain would naturally be considered to have low humanity for example while a noble redcap who is either bound by structural code of conduct or who just uses his/her nightmarish nature to teach valuable lessons to his victims and gains little pleasure from the terror felt by them could have a higher humanity for the purposes of said vampiric power. In the end humanity is just a statistic that measures how monstrous one is. Similar Logic can pretty easily be used in most situations that come up with crossovers.<br /> <br /> Naturally while I have never had problems when it comes to crossovers and in fact to me the very idea of the different lines being their own seperate WoDs is an alien concept as to me WoD has ever been a one world inhabited by all sorts of supernatural beings each with their own perspective on things. To me lupines have always been the Garou it's just that Vampires whom do not generally speak the Garou Tongue wouldn't know to call them that and the leeches have always been the Kindred it's just that the Garou would never use a word that implies such likeness or familiarity to describe such a monstrous, in their eyes, being. But in the end as with all things YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T08:48:34-07:00","id":1113267,"title":"","content":"While I too like troupe play with experienced players (as long as power gamers are kept in check), too many options can be an issue with new players. Also, all those books add up for those new to this hobby of ours.<br /> <br /> However I am pondering detailing fae friendly groups that I think need attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 07-08-2017, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T15:12:21-07:00","id":1113408,"title":"","content":"Easiest fix: there aren't any Prodigals. Just changelings and chimeras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T19:26:42-07:00","id":1113499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1113408#post1113408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easiest fix: there aren't any Prodigals. Just changelings and chimeras.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would certainly make for a colder world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T22:40:11-07:00","id":1113606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1113267#post1113267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I too like troupe play with experienced players (as long as power gamers are kept in check), too many options can be an issue with new players. Also, all those books add up for those new to this hobby of ours.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do understand but then again if the crossover splats are meant to be NPC's you can either use their own systems, if familiar with them as they only work on the background only you need to be aware of them so no confusion for new players, or the systems given for them in C20, if not familiar with the splats in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However I am pondering detailing fae friendly groups that I think need attention. </div> </div> </div>I do understand the sentiment as we have woefully little details on Fae-prodical relations especially with the factions most suited to such things. More information on House Merinita in general, House Fiona and Fianna tribe's relations beyond off-hand mentions of sharing Fae blood would be much appreciated. Similarly information of Kiasyd, and now Maeghar, and their relations to the Fae and Dreaming in general, as Mytheceria allows them to basically enchant themselves and thus make their involment in chimerical matters almost certain. Now that we have been given the Thallain most likely behind the whole Kiasyd affair, in the from of Sevartal, it would be nice to get to know more of their relations, and the Oaths involved in the matter as the Sevartal have almost certainly forged some Oaths between them and Markonius and likely those Oaths could reach to his line as a whole.<br /> Speaking of Oaths it would be very nice to get more information of the Ancient Oaths forged between the Fae and various prodigals, like with the Garou and Fianna specifically.<br /> <br /> But in the end none of this needs particularly mechanical data, as most of what we would need is more fluff information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T06:21:09-07:00","id":1113704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1113408#post1113408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easiest fix: there aren't any Prodigals. Just changelings and chimeras.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think ghosts need to be there too, although they could be more like how ghosts work in Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T07:13:51-07:00","id":1113722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1113704#post1113704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easiest fix: there aren't any Prodigals. Just changelings and chimeras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think ghosts need to be there too, although they could be more like how ghosts work in Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>How Banal can CtD players be if they wish to limit possibilities and eliminate diversion in the world by removing whole species of beings?<br /> <br /> But each to his/her own I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":". 07-09-2017, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T07:22:53-07:00","id":1113727,"title":"","content":"Wow, were insults really called for here? I just think there's enough awesome stuff in Changeling to last a lifetime of gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T08:08:37-07:00","id":1113737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1113727#post1113727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, were insults really called for here? I just think there's enough awesome stuff in Changeling to last a lifetime of gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't an insult. More of statement of the obvious in an ironic manner. I even included an acknowledgement of validity of a differing opinion within my last sentence.<br /> <br /> If you took my statement as an insult I do apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T12:12:49-07:00","id":1113815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1113722#post1113722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How Banal can CtD players be if they wish to limit possibilities and eliminate diversion in the world by removing whole species of beings?<br /> <br /> But each to his/her own I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other game worlds forget Changeling regularly. In fact most of the other lines seem to hate CtD. I was just discussing options for storytellers that dont have all of the books.<br /> <br /> This sort of thing is what made the cWOD a hard sell. And it is still the problem today. These games need to have standalone AND troupe play as possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T12:41:23-07:00","id":1113826,"title":"","content":"Diversity it's overrated. To be Glamorous the elements composing the diversity need to have meaning, otherwise it's as bland as those preprocessed &quot;balanced foods&quot; that have elements of every food but have a dry and homogeneous taste.<br /> <br /> So, since this thread isn't and never was about why crossovering it's evil, but about how to make it less evil. We could think about the meaning, the narrative flavor, that these elements may apport to a Changeling story.<br /> <br /> The basic setting of Changeling it's to stave off Banality and create Glamour. Changelings try to return glamour to the lives of people, to make them dream and create, to return a little of the lost dreamy youth that in adults it's slowly replaced with being jaded, realistic, and practical.<br /> <br /> Changelings also have to face nightmares and some of the crazines of the Dreaming (while office buildings are the main antagonist, they aren't the only one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> Changeling has the potential to be almost as gonzo as Mage, but it's core themes are much more intimist than those of Mage, or any other game for what matters. Faes really have interact with humanity at a very intimate level to survive.<br /> <br /> Or I am wrong? If I'm not wrong, I think it may be worthy to think about how other supernaturals figure in all of this:<br /> <br /> Yes, you could try to inspire a Toreador to create art...but leaving this at that doesn't really adress how a Toreador it's different from any human. You could go to a human artist and inspire her with much less risk to your blood...<br /> <br /> Sure, a Ventrue may try to build an office where the freehold it's, but so can any human corporation.<br /> <br /> How can we bring the themes of vampire to the fae's table?. How can we bring the themes of the other games?<br /> <br /> Ideas:<br /> <br /> As antagonist: Perhaps the Toreador has decided to ghoul some humans that were interesting to PC faes. Perhaps by ghouling an interesting mortal the Toreador it's, unknowingly, breaking a story of true love that a fae was trying to make happen to create Glamour. This involves blood bond and the predatory nature of vampires in a way that can't be ignored or trully replicated with purely human elements, I think.<br /> <br /> As ally: This one it's a bit trickier, as vampires tend to be very Banal. What if a vampire was known to the fae in a past live. Perhaps the Toreador was an artist with an incredible potential, or something like that. This potential has been lost to the ages, of ourse, but maybe a character can try to lit it back.<br /> <br /> With Mage the core of the average game it's about hope against all the odds, freedom vs security, faith.<br /> <br /> As ally: Instead of inspiring a Mage to create a work of art, a fae could inspire a mage to do a Great Work. Mages are people who thrive to change their surroundings, they are here to shape reality and they have the great willpower to do it. An inteligent fae could use this by providing the <i>vision </i>they need.<br /> Traditionalist mages are very Glamorous, their Magick it's described in all Changeling books as something of Glamour. They're natural alies to faes in a fight against conformism. Technocrats would never do this, knowingly.<br /> <br /> As antagonists:<br /> While mages of Mage don't have a largue story of antagonizing the fae (the contrary it's usually true), in real life myths it happened.<br /> As an example: the myth that depicts the fall of the Tuatha De Danann at the hands of the ancestors of the Irish people, the Millesians, had the Millesian poet Amergin stop a magical storm conjured by the Tuatha. Amergin played a pivotal role in the defeat of the mythical race ensuring the dominance of &quot;humanity&quot; over the island.<br /> In real life myth wizards often had the means to undo the shenanigans of the fae or were able to turn the arcane rules of the faes against them.<br /> <br /> In WoD some mages have the means to recognize faes as what they really are, and maybe they want to eradicate them based on superstitions or fact that depict fae as dangerous (if the PC are of the Unseelie, maybe the mage it's right), or could want to hunt or control the PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-09-2017, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T13:41:51-07:00","id":1113861,"title":"","content":"Vampires being inherently Banal has thankfully been removed in C20. So you can now do stories like fighting over a Dreamer, in a way where Kithain (or Vampire from the other end) society cannot help resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T14:54:29-07:00","id":1113882,"title":"","content":"The Ravnos make for awesome villains to CtD thanks to their discipline imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:43:58-07:00","id":1113908,"title":"","content":"The primary issue with crossovers was the relative power level (the Dreaming is its own thing, but it connects to every level of the Unbra, so there are no real conflicts). I honestly prefer CtD to MtAs, as there is less power gaming, and because CtD is much easier to crossover than MtAs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T21:33:59-07:00","id":1114039,"title":"","content":"As someone who does like my worlds of darkness (old and new) seperated into nice thematic and cosmological bubbles I really like dreaming being it's own thing.<br /> <br /> I've always wanted to see something with dreaming mages as Enchanters. As in the one's who found their innate connection to the dreaming to enchant themselves perpetually. After all humanity shapes the dreaming unconsciously so one who can do it consciously would basically be... well a wizard. This allows them to call on the dreaming and bring back magic in their own ways. I've often considered whether to use arts and realms for them or whether to steal the old faith powers from dark ages mage, nerfed by banality. It even fits thematically as the coming of Winter would snuff out the magic in humanity so they have every reason to help the fey... or the fomorians who may promise to let them preserve their power in the coming age","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 07-10-2017, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T12:47:34-07:00","id":1114244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1114039#post1114039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who does like my worlds of darkness (old and new) seperated into nice thematic and cosmological bubbles I really like dreaming being it's own thing.<br /> <br /> I've always wanted to see something with dreaming mages as Enchanters. As in the one's who found their innate connection to the dreaming to enchant themselves perpetually. After all humanity shapes the dreaming unconsciously so one who can do it consciously would basically be... well a wizard. This allows them to call on the dreaming and bring back magic in their own ways. I've often considered whether to use arts and realms for them or whether to steal the old faith powers from dark ages mage, nerfed by banality. It even fits thematically as the coming of Winter would snuff out the magic in humanity so they have every reason to help the fey... or the fomorians who may promise to let them preserve their power in the coming age</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> THIS is the sort of thing I was hoping to discuss. And I LOVE the concept of the Enchanter as a kind of Dream-tapping magician. A Hedge Magic society from the old Sorcerer book comes to mind:<br /> <br /> <b>Zolondrodere: The Dreamers of the Silver Portal</b><br /> A recent revival of an ancient group, the Dreamers of the Silver Star are oneiromancers \u2013 magicians whose powers lie in dreams and the Dreaming. This fellowship of seven sorcerers base their magics on the Covenent of the Silver Portal, an 18<sup>th</sup> century English translation of a 14<sup>th</sup> century Byzantium Greek manuscript which in turn was translated from a 5<sup>th</sup> century Persian scroll that may in fact be translated from another ancient work. This single tome purports to reveal the secrets of oneiromancy and the hidden terrain of the dream worlds \u2013 the Dream Realms called Maya, from which, it is said, all magics come.<br /> The Dreamers of the Silver Portal gather together in dreamform and traverse the byways of the Dreaming, in search of the fabled City of Syrannon \u2013 a city that, if found, grants the dreamer life eternal. Many dreamers have gone mad on such a quest, discovering instead otherworldly horrors and the nightmares of dying gods. Some few have returned from their slumber enriched by savage insights and possessed on unearthly gifts.<br /> Who can question the nature of dreams?<br /> <b>Paths:</b> Conveyance, Fascination, Healing, Oneiromancy (required). <br /> <br /> If you want to avoid using <a href=\"http://z6.invisionfree.com/Masquerade_Project/ar/t3741.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Hedge Magic</a> paths, I could see just granting these guys Arts and Realms. Or perhaps *just* the Art of <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oneiromancy. Heck, a Mortal with Kenning and Gremayre has the potential to be potent dreamer. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:44:38-07:00","id":1114259,"title":"","content":"not a bad idea, and yeah hedge magic is fairly good though it may require tweaking to specifically work with chimera and the dreaming, and using bunks is the kind of thing I love seeing in a magic system so letting the paths work more like realms is not something i'd be averse to.<br /> <br /> perhaps worth it to bring back 1e sorcerer's emphemera reskinned and adjusted for the dreaming and perhaps an astral projection power for dream travel (would they have chimera stats in that form?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T13:55:58-07:00","id":1114265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1114259#post1114259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not a bad idea, and yeah hedge magic is fairly good though it may require tweaking to specifically work with chimera and the dreaming, and using bunks is the kind of thing I love seeing in a magic system so letting the paths work more like realms is not something i'd be averse to.<br /> <br /> perhaps worth it to bring back 1e sorcerer's emphemera reskinned and adjusted for the dreaming and perhaps an astral projection power for dream travel (would they have chimera stats in that form?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemera could easily be reskinned for the Dreaming. Use Kenning and Gremayre for the abilities and deal with Chimera and Fae instead of wraiths and such, and there you go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:02:28-07:00","id":1114739,"title":"","content":"I will acknowledge that CtD is often forgotten about in crossover discussions elsewhere. That said, I have had a crossover game involving mostly cWoD Mages, nWoD Vampires, nWoD Werewolves, and changelings (a little bit) based on CtD. We had very few/no problems. There was also a homebrewed &quot;Highlander&quot; style Immortal character (with enemies of course). I will note that the mechanics were converted to nWoD (first edition, before it got renamed CofD)<br /> <br /> I realize that the conventional attitude on these forums and reddit is that crossovers are terrible for cWoD, but I have never had a problem with it in several years of playing with one ST. My newest ST has stated that he has never had problems with it either, and my recollection is that he ran a CtD game primarily with some Mage PCs (his crossover was entirely cWoD).<br /> <br /> It's hard to say who're more powerful. I guess Mages at the fourth dot in spheres probably beat out Changelings with their fourth dot in an Art (even if powerful). The fifth dot for Mage spheres is also insanely powerful, but so are the fifth dots for Changelings. Yes, Mages have way more flexibility. But Changelings, if they can overcome banality (yes, a potentially huge hurdle), don't have the same blink-you-out-of-existence risk of paradox that Mages have when working those higher dot effects.<br /> <br /> There is also a huge constraint in Mage: the Ascension games that is hard to deal with in crossover, which is the Technocracy. Even if I don't blink myself out of existence or (with the less disastrous result) actually kill myself with paradox, the Techoncracy is going to be up my ass. Managing that in a way that does not penalize the Changelings in the group could be done but is not super easy.<br /> <br /> I think I recall somewhere in one of the Changeling books (maybe even the 2nd edition core rulebook?) some examples of doing Mages with Changeling powers (or Changeling-like ones) instead of using their rules, if desired.<br /> <br /> As far as the banality ratings for Mage belief systems (e.g., the true mystics such as the Verbena in contrast with true believers such as the Celestial Chorus), I think those are a generally good guideline. But as mentioned previously, Avatars are important. A very dynamic/Questing essence Technocrat should be more banal than a similarly dynamic Tradition mage, so perhaps that Technocrat gets to be a 7 or <i>maybe</i> a 6 (maybe).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:36:59-07:00","id":1114785,"title":"","content":"Changelings also get a major power bump in C20 (well, sort of, they're also harder to min-max now, but most STs wouldn't want that sort of thing at the table). When I said I think they're probably fine mixed with Mages now I meant with C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T17:58:32-07:00","id":1114834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1114785#post1114785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings also get a major power bump in C20 (well, sort of, they're also harder to min-max now, but most STs wouldn't want that sort of thing at the table). When I said I think they're probably fine mixed with Mages now I meant with C20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very happy to hear this. Changelings were such glass jaws in previous editions. A fae magician should be powerful.<br /> <br /> I guess I am hoping for a CtD version of Ascensions Right Hand. An assortment of options for n fae companions and foes. Enchanters, Chimera, Fae Animals etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T18:50:03-07:00","id":1114851,"title":"","content":"I've never had a problem mixing other games into my Changeling ones, though I've only done it as NPCs. I don't think that a chronicle with mixed PCs would work well because of the big issue with non-Kithain perceiving and interacting with chimerical reality. With NPCs I can fudge a little, make them enchanted, etc., and have never had an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T16:38:22-07:00","id":1117998,"title":"","content":"I can see NPCs being easier to integrate, but mixing various PCs from various splats can work well with a bit of ST and player coordination. The first thing to do would be to determine which is the 'main game' or splat. If it's Changeling, then your Werewolf tribes probably should be Fianna, maybe the Silver Fangs, possibly the Children of Gaia, or one other tribes that gets mentioned a fair amount in Changeling source material that currently I don't recall. And their choice of powers should include abilities that enable them to interact easily with Changelings and their world. A similar thing would be needed for a Mage character (any of them likely would need Spirit at a minimum of 1, with a preference for 2, and possibly Changeling and/or Dreaming Lore, etc.). Prime likely would be a good idea as well. For Vampires, perhaps Malkavians and/or having Auspex would be necessary (though perhaps Vampires do not mix well at all, absent a specific Changeling PC group composition that seeks out interaction with Vampires). <br /> <br /> If the main game is not Changeling, then a Sidhe character interested primarily in Fae court politics might have to shift their focus to politics between Changelings and other supernatural groups in the area (think the setup they have for Santa Cruz in Changeling's source material). They will have to realize that aside from a few solo scenes (or perhaps solo sessions, if the ST and that player have time), internal politics won't be a focus for the chronicle.<br /> <br /> I do think more coordination ahead of time is required for Changeling as a main game. We had an oWoD crossover featuring mostly Mages with a Vampire that worked just fine (though the Vampire didn't get many chances to interact with Vampire society), a nWoD game with oWoD Mage setting but nWoD Vampire and nWoD Werewolf PCs (and an otherwise nWoD setting), and that worked fine.<br /> <br /> The worst crossover (beyond a very short-term chronicle) I can think of likely would be Prometheans from nWoD, actually. I don't know if they released a second edition, but based on the first edition, Prometheans being around anyone (including supernaturals) for any significant amount of time eventually spells disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T16:57:04-07:00","id":1118001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imperator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1117998#post1117998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The worst crossover (beyond a very short-term chronicle) I can think of likely would be Prometheans from nWoD, actually. I don't know if they released a second edition, but based on the first edition, Prometheans being around anyone (including supernaturals) for any significant amount of time eventually spells disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean 2E is out. Prometheans still cause disaster, but more from carelessness or desperation or stagnation, rather than inevitability or mundane daily life. So there's more agency for the players.<br /> <br /> I'd say a worse crossover is the two Changeling games, since they have <i>very </i>different ideas on what fairies are, and from there the two games' themes would start to deviate. (Not sure on the latter, since I don't know enough about Dreaming's themes for sure.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T05:35:50-07:00","id":1118139,"title":"","content":"I have to agree (plus the nature of the Dreaming and Changeling magic are radically different).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T10:56:06-07:00","id":1118215,"title":"","content":"I've run a mixed game for years. Most of the players are either changelings it Fera, and I've had little to no problems. Even power scale wise. I will admit to throwing the changelings a few more XP towards Arts early on, but that made them quite...terrifying in battle. A Werewolf might by a walking blender, but a changeling with a few well placed cantrips will completely hamstring the opposing bad guys. <br /> <br /> The one house rule that I did have to decide on was changelings being immune to delirium and werewolves mostly being free from negative effects of long-term enchantment.<br /> <br /> What results from their integration, I find, is a very dynamic game of beige of hope caring for the fragile psyche of creatures in a constant state of despair. We've had some beautiful as well as chilling scenes as as result. <br /> <br /> There was also the incident of the 'Ensnair - with - silver - piano - wire'...but we shall not dwell on that...never let a pooka plan ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T20:01:41-07:00","id":1118376,"title":"","content":"Personally I like the variety in the WoD and have never had a problem with crossovers. In my Changeling games I've had werewolves, mages, vampires, and wraiths as NPCs, all without any issues. I don't delve too much in the game mechanics since they're NPCs, but I don't deviate too much from the source material. I even had a werewolf develop into a love interest for an eshu PC, and it worked out well. Only once did I have a mixed PC group, with a werewolf (Fianna) joining the kithain, but with that tribe it's pretty easy to justify as the garou can be kinain.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T03:59:23-07:00","id":1118472,"title":"","content":"Throw out pre-packaged ratings of Banality and go with your gut. <br /> <br /> Think of Banality as a spectrum for every individual Changeling, Mortal or Prodigal to fit in somewhere, based on their individual circumstances and experiences and not determined solely by their assossiated groups.<br /> <br /> Have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:48:30-07:00","id":1118643,"title":"","content":"Luckily C20 threw out the pre-packaged Banality ratings as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:01:36-07:00","id":1118695,"title":"","content":"...........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":".  Double posted 07-20-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T19:06:37-07:00","id":1125451,"title":"","content":"Had some thoughts on other templates being redone as apart of changeling. I mentioned enchanters before, now for werewolves<br /> <br /> Sir Marrok was a Fae Blooded knight in service to a seelie lord long before the sundering. He served his lord well and was given a blessing tied to his knightly oaths. He gained a chimeric form through magics long lost to the Fae. When Sir Marrok's wife became ill he went to her to stay with her as she lay dying however when he did so assassin's crept upon his unguarded lord and slew him. His oaths broken Sir Marrok's blessing became a curse, his lupine form becoming twisted and driving him mad. Worse still his oaths bound not just him but all of his bloodline. His name became lost in time and woven into other legends. His descendants, now bound by the light of the moon become craven beasts under the full moon light hunting and killing those who smell of fear, their crimes hidden by the mists. But all is not lost for the oaths remain in effect and any of Marrok's descendants may renew those oaths to another lord of the sidhe and have their curse become a blessing once more.<br /> <br /> Mechanically these werewolves are Fae Blooded who bear the blood of Marrok. They may spend one willpower to create a chimeric form of a large wolflike humanoid, that has the stat adjustments of a garou crinos form making them quite powerful. Under the light of the full moon they automatically enter this form while calling on the wyrd, allowing it to effect the mortal world. While in this form they are savage hunters preying on the fearful, unable to maintain rational thought. By making an oath of fealty to a sidhe lord they may negate this effect, giving them full control of their faculties while in their lupine form, they no longer shift automatically and may enter the form in a wyrd state at will once per month, refreshing during the full moon.<br /> <br /> (it should be noted i do not have C20 yet and thus don't have rules for the fae blooded, i may amend this once the book is out on DTRPG)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T05:44:37-07:00","id":1125561,"title":"","content":"I've never done crossovers because I think they would ruin the game atmosphere. I mean, Changelings are creatures that walk a tightrope between believing and not believing what they are. It's like the &quot;Pan's Labyrinth&quot;: Ophelia doesn't have a full proof that she is a princess, but if you believe, you can see evidences (fragile evidences). <br /> In CtD it gets worse: if you believe too much you can go to Bedlam, but if you start doubting too much, you risk go to ruin.<br /> When you do crossovers, your character deals with people that are alive for the last centuries or can shapeshift into a killer bestial machine. I cannot imagine how this changeling could doubt that she is a fairy trapped in a human body, so I think this could easily change the game's atmosphere.<br /> Well, that's totally ok if its YOUR wish, but keep in mind that there are a lot of rules and drama that lacks sense if you do that. In the end, it's an issue that requires more thinking that just dealing with rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","user":"Neon.Sidhe","date":". 08-06-2017, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:51:41-07:00","id":1128313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings#post1112862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We all know crossovers stink. And the different groups populating the classic World of Darkness all have their own mechanics, most of which dont mesh with Changeling.<br /> <br /> Personally, I handle the other types of beings as denizens of the Dreaming (vampires, werecritters, etc) or mortals with enough knowledge of magic to be dangerous (hedge magic and/or Arts n Realms).<br /> <br /> What house rules do you use?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It was my understanding that while the different supernaturals exist at the same time, they're not the same incarnations of them between splats. As in, the Werewolves in Masquerade are not the same Werewolves in Apocalypse, and so on.<br /> <br /> Though if this is not the case, then I've been mislead.<br /> <br /> <br /> My house rule would be that the other splats have about as much in depth knowledge on the other splats as hunters have about each of them. Namely being their strengths and weaknesses, but nothing about their internal workings and philosophies. They're too busy dealing with their own crap to go poking around in each others' businesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T20:03:17-07:00","id":1128315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1128313#post1128313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It was my understanding that while the different supernaturals exist at the same time, they're not the same incarnations of them between splats. As in, the Werewolves in Masquerade are not the same Werewolves in Apocalypse, and so on.<br /> <br /> Though if this is not the case, then I've been mislead.<br /> <br /> <br /> My house rule would be that the other splats have about as much in depth knowledge on the other splats as hunters have about each of them. Namely being their strengths and weaknesses, but nothing about their internal workings and philosophies. They're too busy dealing with their own crap to go poking around in each others' businesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>It completely depends on the supplement and sometimes sections within the supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T14:43:51-07:00","id":1262738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1118643#post1118643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luckily C20 threw out the pre-packaged Banality ratings as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to hear it. Vampires being Banal was one point of consistency for Werewolf/Changeling crossover. Kindred Banality was based on the fact that Vampires are by their very nature static and unchanging -- i.e., of the Weaver -- and changing that just threw that idea out the window.<br /> <br /> Which I hope they are consistent about in Werewolf, then, for crossover; not all Vampires are Weaver. Being static and unchanging does not = Weaver. Ergo, it does not, in a crossover sense, equal Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","name":"Observer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T15:32:13-07:00","id":1262752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Observer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1262738#post1262738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry to hear it. Vampires being Banal was one point of consistency for Werewolf/Changeling crossover. Kindred Banality was based on the fact that Vampires are by their very nature static and unchanging -- i.e., of the Weaver -- and changing that just threw that idea out the window.<br /> <br /> Which I hope they are consistent about in Werewolf, then, for crossover; not all Vampires are Weaver. Being static and unchanging does not = Weaver. Ergo, it does not, in a crossover sense, equal Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Weaver isn't necessarily Banal either, nor is the Wyld necessarily low Banality. And saying it was never fit with Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T19:44:24-07:00","id":1262785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1112862-changeling-the-dreaming-without-the-other-settings?p=1262752#post1262752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Weaver isn't necessarily Banal either, nor is the Wyld necessarily low Banality. And saying it was never fit with Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd tend to disagree on Weaver not being Banal, seeing as it represents stasis and the status quo. Not sure how Wyld could be other than low banality, but.<br /> <br /> And yes, it was more of a griping because, while I haven't read C20, I am in crossover games currently, and it worked in both cosmologies. Wyrm doesn't exactly exist in Changeling, but they recognize Fomori and Thallain as corrupt and 'inimical to the Dreaming', even if they are part of it. Destroyers. So, they might register as Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Glamour and changelings are capricious and not entirely sane and predictable = Wyld.<br /> Banality is what happens when Changelings begin to lose the spark of creativity and belief, and grow more fixed in their ways and thinking = Weaver.<br /> <br /> Worked beautifully, and I wish/hope the newer games would be more crossover-friendly and consider all angles with reasoned arguments before changing things that would contradict other cosmologies or even its own earlier editions, like deciding vampires are no longer banal by nature. How can you suddenly explain some Vampires being creative (Even creating Glamour or Wyld), while still being 'Weaver' to Sense Weaver in werewolf due to their fixed and unchanging natures? It doesn't compute -- to me, it makes as much sense as saying 'Some Autumn People are Dreamers'.<br /> <br /> Even Mage has different Avatars, like Static, Dynamic, and Primordial, with Technocracy tending towards Static (no coincidence they are extremely Banal). So it was one of the few threads that ran through each game that was A) Both a vital component of the cosmology and B) Made them compatible. Werewolves and Changelings could have common antagonists, because the spread of the Weaver corresponded with the spread of Banality, etc.<br /> <br /> I might make its own thread on this a bit later, I just realized this feels a bit like hijacking, if I go further into the details of why I think this is so, and so on. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24663,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","user":"Observer","date":". 10-25-2018, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","name":"Observer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T20:16:46-07:00","id":1262788,"title":"","content":"C20 made Glamour/Banality less objective and more subjective compared to past editions.<br /> <br /> That now what is/isn't Glamorous or Banal is going to vary a lot more from changeling to changeling. So while that Technocrat's lab might be Banal to that pooka, that nocker might thrive in that environment. While the stuffy courtly politicking by that Ventrue Prince might seem appalling to the piskey, maybe not for the Unseelie Arcadian sidhe lord.<br /> <br /> It allows more flexibility for potential PCs and stories you could tell, which is only a net-win for everyone.<br /> <br /> ...for instance, to me it never made sense that the Resurgence was kickstarted by a scientific milestone, and yet by 1e-2e definitions, that SHOULD have been Banal because at that point &quot;science = Banal&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-25T20:30:44-07:00","id":1262791,"title":"","content":"Well, stasis isn't Banality either. Banality is more about holding back from what you want to do in your heart and instead conforming to what society wants from you. Depending on who you are and what society is like how that plays into the Triat can be quite different. In that lab example, it's Banality raiting would depend on how many researchers are there because it's their life's pasion, and how many are there because it's a paycheque they can earn with the degree their parents wanted them to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T21:35:55-07:00","id":1303003,"title":"","content":"Ooh, this is my kind of topic. A bit of a rant first, though, just to set down my philosophy...<br /> <br /> Now... changeling suffers the problem of being the last game in the line. So, what crossover material is presented comes with the pre-existence of the other splats set up already. Vampire didn't have this problem early on since they were the first, and even as the other lines formed, they often were able to frame the other supernaturals in very vague forms. Even in the BNS LARP rules for vampire, made around the same time as V20, they provided loose templates for other supernaturals as NPCs, but provided very little in actual lore - the Werewolves fight the Wyrm and see the vampires as part of it, the Mages get the Order of Hermes namedropped because of the Tremere (and to be fair the Order of Hermes technically predates VtM with Ars Magica) and nothing else (the sample NPCs have a hint of the power ratings and name the spheres - &quot;Disciple of Mind and Life,&quot; and the enigmatic &quot;Master of Dark Prime&quot; who had Ash Path Necromancy and Obtenebration, meaning that Dark Prime could be the Nephandic Prime or could be the Underworld or Abyss - which exist in the VtM world in loose terms through the Giovanni, Cappadocians, and Lasombra, but are not as defined as the Umbra is in the WtA book - or could be both; there isn't a built-in lore to those terms that is elaborated in-game though). VtM just tends to go &quot;here are these monsters and a loose bit of story about them, and some disciplines that sorta kinda could be their powers; have fun.&quot; But, as the games go on, when they want to feature other supernatural antagonists, they have more established lore to work with - which can lead to some overfocusing and unnecessary (and possibly contradictory) crossing of the streams. In the earliest version of WtA, the Setites had just been introduced to the VtM world. The Striders were nomads and wanderers, but didn't have a specific connection to their now-universal enemy. But, the BNS Werewolf book, using the same sort of stock system as the VtM (for those who haven't played, Stock NPCs have a dot rating and a number of specialties equal to that rating; those specialties can be skills or powers/powersets, with the powers being at the rating of the stock character - quick and easy way to design NPCs), but going into far more detail about the &quot;vampires&quot; drawn up as antagonists - where the VtM book had a healer shaman type and a warrior, the WtA book had a Tzimisce Sabbat Ductus (Elder, no less), a Toreador Cammie, an Anarch Gangrel, and my personal bane, a Malkavian &quot;Scion of Ankou.&quot; I had to dig through the tradition books just to find out about the Ankou, who gets no mention in the VtM book. That is some deep lore - like, need a rorqual to get you there deep). Even in older books, though, you saw this with the werewolves having more specific ties to vampires than vice versa. So it can be a bit harder to separate out what is presented in the book completely.<br /> <br /> My personal strategy is, use what is there, and make up the rest. You can have there be something called &quot;the Technocratic Union&quot; but it isn't necessarily the collection of conventions we see today. It could be a monolithic cyborg factory. It could be a fractious group of mecha-cultists under the guise of a &quot;union.&quot; It can be what we want it to be, because it is just a name and a description (though, I did just see mention of a &quot;Void Engineer&quot; in C20. Sigh.)<br /> <br /> So, while I love the C20 science =/= banality thing, as well as the overall de-villainizing of the Technocrats overtime, I do think that the &quot;technocrats,&quot; as described in the 2E Core and 20th Anniversary edition should remain as the antagonist and still remain as Banal as hell. They may not be overtly hostile, but their nature and magic hurts. They fuel their powers with Banality instead of Glamour. Conversely, the rest of the mages are divided into the categories used in the game: Maruaders, the mystic storms of Bedlam and wild magic; the Mystics, holders to the ancient ways; the True Believers, who are powerful in glamour but whose glamour may be tainted by their beliefs, and the Cynics, who are sort of banal but can have their eyes open. The Sahajiya mentioned in C20 are just a cult - a friendly cult, but not one of the &quot;nine major traditions.&quot; The Toreador, Kiasyd, and Ravnos are among the vampires in the world, but anything else could exist.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of just using the powers in the book as the powers for all the supernaturals. As mentioned, it does allow room to turn a supernatural type into a splat for the game - an enchanter, or even a Sahajiya Cultist kith, could be real fun to play, but would stay in the line of power for the template. And, thanks to Unleashing, I can simulate mage magic a good bit more easily.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... may need make birthrights and a frailty for the Sahajiya..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}